# Theme BR deploy workaround — temporarily permit
# packages/core/{dist,.tshy-build} so webapp Dockerfile's transitive
# build skips the CJS tshy pass that swallows its tsc error on
# low-RAM Docker builders. Everywhere else these dirs stay ignored.
!packages/core/dist
!packages/core/dist/**
!packages/core/.tshy-build
!packages/core/.tshy-build/**

**/generated/prisma

apps/webapp/build
apps/webapp/public/build

cypress/screenshots
cypress/videos

apps/**/styles/tailwind.css
packages/**/styles/tailwind.css

.changeset
.DS_Store
.git
.github
.idea
.pnp
.pnp.js
.vscode

coverage
build
# /-anchored so only the top-level docs/ + examples/ are excluded.
# Without the leading /, the unanchored pattern also caught content/docs/
# which silently broke the docs+guides pipeline at deploy time (Phase 3b).
/docs/*
!/docs/control-plane-parity.generated.md
# The agent image build runs `build:platos:agent`, whose `build:strict` step runs
# `generate-control-plane.mjs --check`. That script and the module it imports read
# exactly two repository files out of the otherwise-excluded /docs/*, and without
# them the image fails at Dockerfile:42 with ENOENT. Enumerated from the path
# constants of every script in apps/agent/scripts, not from a grep for literals:
#   generate-control-plane.mjs:36  errorTaxonomyPath
#   openapi-meta-schema.mjs:59     META_SCHEMA_PATH
!/docs/error-taxonomy.json
!/docs/openapi-3.1-meta-schema.json
/examples
out

CHANGESETS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md
# LICENSE and NOTICE are deliberately NOT excluded: Apache-2.0 s4(a) requires
# every recipient of a distributed work to receive a copy of the License, and
# s4(d) requires the NOTICE attributions to travel with it. Shipped images are a
# distribution, so both files must reach the build context and be COPYed into
# the final stage of every image.

# WIN-291 — host-level edge/runbook material must never enter the build context.
# apps/agent/Dockerfile uses `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is shipped
# into the image builder. /deploy and /hosting hold edge routing + runbooks.
/deploy
/hosting

# Agent worktrees are created INSIDE the repo at .claude/worktrees/. Without this
# they re-enter the build context carrying a full second copy of the tree.
/.claude
